    {
     "label": "D",
     "text": "999"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "B",
   "solution": "![B Since 8 and 9 do not have a common factor, a number that is a common multiple of 8 and 9 is a multiple of = 8 × 9 8 × 9 = 72 Multiples of 72: 72 .... 720, 792, 864, 936, 1008 ... Greatest 3 - digit number that is a common multiple of 8 and 9 = 936](asset:q2-sol)",
